The critical group of a directed graph (https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0010241)
citeturn0academia20 [wordlim: 200] Published: 26.1 years ago; The critical group K(G) of a directed graph G=(V,E) is the cokernel of the transpose of the Laplacian matrix of G acting on the integer lattice Z^V. For undirected graphs G, this has been considered by Bacher, de la Harpe, and Nagnibeda, and by Biggs.
